ver  the overdraft of the government and  borrowing for public investment you know  building up an infrastructure in our  broadband railways housing and the  government could be getting on with that  borrowing at very very low rates of  interest in order to build up the  country and they keep more productive  than this Tory government isn't doing it  so you you mentioned there that the toys  are starting to grapple with the idea of  higher taxation would you support higher  taxation well I think it's going to have  to happen whoever is in government and  the question is how you do it and making  sure you do it in a fair way I mean  where I would start is some of the  changes that the Conservatives are  brought in since we left the coalition  them and why on earth are we cutting  corporation tax it's well well below the  average of developing im9 pro-business I  mean I want to see business investing  but all that's happening is that  businesses are pocketing the money and  they're sitting on it they're not  investing in it because of all the  uncertainty around brexit that we need  to make the UK an attractive place  prospective I want I want written to be  an attractive place to invest in but  that is unnecessary and it is very very  expensive so you support Jeremy Corbyn  then in saying that corporation tax  should be looked at well certainly on  that particular point I'm not sure I'd  go along with all of jeremy corbyn's  ideas on tax but on that yes definitely  now and before you go I'm quite  interested to know you've had two years  away from politics now have you found it  have you been filling your time if you  take up gardening are you watching box  sets into the small hours not gardening  no I'm not great in the garden  but I've been writing books I've got a  novel appearing in august-september I'm  working universities including my local  university and Twickenham and the London  School of Economics is what you do in  your downtime I still give them up to m